      <ownedAttribute xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193376_336377_24613" xmi:uuid="b97432df-7759-49b2-8ae2-cb130b69c48f" xmi:type="uml:Property">
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_0_5_45e01bd_1455707929808_819977_42753" xmi:uuid="916fade8-0921-4579-9b35-6c56384a8ff5" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193376_336377_24613"/>
          <body> the text that specifies the meaning of the relationship. Where applicable, the following values shall be used: &lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;'decomposition': The Related Approval is one of the components into which the Relating Approval is broken down with no implication of 'sequence' or 'dependency'; &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;'dependency': The issuing of the Related Approval is dependent on the issuing of the Relating Approval; &lt;note&gt; The value 'dependency' does not imply the semantics of the values 'decomposition' or 'sequence'. &lt;/note&gt;&lt;example&gt; The Approval of an assembly may be dependent on the Approval of all of the constituents of the assembly. &lt;/example&gt;&lt;example&gt; In two parallel sequences of Approval objects for two assemblies a certain Approval object of one assembly may be dependent on a certain Approval object of the second assembly. &lt;/example&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;'precedence': The Related Approval has higher priority than the Relating Approval; &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;'sequence': The Relating Approval shall be completed before the Related Approval is given.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt; </body>
        </ownedComment>
        <name>RelationType</name>
        <visibility>public</visibility>
        <type href="../CommonResources/CommonResources.xmi#_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193042_855579_23449"/>
        <association xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193374_161360_24604"/>
      </ownedAttribute>
