    </packagedElement>
    <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193259_743259_23866" xmi:uuid="1fd0747e-202c-4579-8903-4f255bc7b7f6" xmi:type="uml:Class">
      <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_0_5_45e01bd_1455121544081_546390_42671" xmi:uuid="91ac47dd-ae7d-479a-a3c6-6ac2b912625e" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
        <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193259_743259_23866"/>
        <body>A SuppliedObjectRelationship is a relationship between two objects of the SuppliedObjectSelect list representing the same object in different organizational contexts. &lt;note&gt; The different organizational contexts can be represented by different OrganizationOrPersonInOrganizationAssignments. &lt;/note&gt;&lt;note&gt; The concept of multi-identification may also be used to distinguish objects in different organizational contexts. However, SuppliedObjectRelationship shall be used if the related object corresponds to an object at the supplier's site and if a distinction of additional information such as name or organizational information is needed. &lt;/note&gt;&lt;example&gt;Usually, PartVersions that are provided by suppliers have at the supplier's site an id different from the one at the contractor's site: a PartVersion that is identified in a company by the identifier 'C425' and the version id 'V2.0' may correspond to the PartVersion that the supplier identifies as '2X45' with the version id 'V3.2'.&lt;/example&gt; </body>
      </ownedComment>
      <name>SuppliedObjectRelationship</name>
      <ownedRule xmi:id="_18_0_5_45e01bd_1459332374174_217157_42733" xmi:uuid="e6434213-82c0-4675-bafa-d181f6d10f3f" xmi:type="uml:Constraint">
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1671462045344_771166_163079" xmi:uuid="1f10a3af-0292-45c6-8c30-1e1eb7dc3cac" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1671462052892_688583_163080" xmi:uuid="37387169-9edd-41f6-aa0b-13d26026930e" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
            <body>WR1: TYPEOF(Relating) = TYPEOF(Related);</body>
          </ownedComment>
          <body>EXPRESS</body>
        </ownedComment>
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_0_5_45e01bd_1459332412201_902243_42735" xmi:uuid="6655d4a8-0757-4e2b-97ca-a3fc3d7ad56b" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_0_5_45e01bd_1459332374174_217157_42733"/>
          <body> the Related and the Relating object shall be of same type.</body>
        </ownedComment>
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1721730196879_993696_153321" xmi:uuid="a632ead7-89f1-48ab-b6ef-b7af72743c98" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1721730196880_51026_153322" xmi:uuid="91ea12b1-6fd3-4d5f-872e-d44be8dea306" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
            <body> &lt;sch:rule context="//SuppliedObjectRelationship[@uid]"&gt; &lt;sch:let name="entity_name" value="if(@xsi:type) then substring-after(@xsi:type,':') else name()"/&gt; &lt;sch:let name="uid" value="@uid"/&gt; &lt;sch:let name="relating_type" value="if(../@xsi:type) then substring-after(../@xsi:type,':') else ../name()"/&gt; &lt;sch:let name="reference_uidRef" value="Related/@uidRef"/&gt; &lt;sch:let name="reference" value="//*[@uid = $reference_uidRef]"/&gt; &lt;sch:let name="related_type" value="if($reference/@xsi:type) then substring-after($reference/@xsi:type,':') else $reference/name()"/&gt; &lt;sch:assert test="$relating_type = $related_type"&gt; The Related and the Relating object shall be of same type. { -entity_name:&lt;sch:value-of select="$entity_name"/&gt; -entity_uid:&lt;sch:value-of select="$uid"/&gt; -rule_name:WR1 -relating_type:&lt;sch:value-of select="$relating_type"/&gt; -related_type:&lt;sch:value-of select="$related_type"/&gt; } &lt;/sch:assert&gt; &lt;/sch:rule&gt;</body>
          </ownedComment>
          <body>Schematron</body>
        </ownedComment>
        <name>WR1</name>
