    <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193130_22342_23621" xmi:uuid="9d62d28b-213f-4018-84e6-45ef4030bf76" xmi:type="uml:Class">
      <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_0_5_45e01bd_1455111762956_868537_42346" xmi:uuid="83510c41-e35b-4f8e-848e-32067904e7d4" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
        <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193130_22342_23621"/>
        <body>An InformationUsageRightAssignment is an assignment of a specific usage right to a set of items. &lt;note&gt; If an Approval is applied to this entity, it carries the meaning that the specific set of items is approved for the given usage. This approval generally indicates that the approval is exceptional and there is an implication that the set of entities should not be changed once the approval is given.&lt;/note&gt;&lt;note&gt; The following additional data can be assigned to an InformationUsageRightAssignment: ActivityMethod, Approval, Condition, DateTimeString, Document, DocumentVersion, DocumentDefinition, File, Effectivity, PropertyValue, ExternalPropertyDefinition, and PropertyDefinition.&lt;/note&gt;</body>
      </ownedComment>
      <name>InformationUsageRightAssignment</name>
